  "details": "<p>As with the other buildings in Sidi Khiribech, the ruins look to have been refurbished and rebuilt at least several times during their lifetime. A public use (possibly baths?) has been suggested by some scholars.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The ruins of an ancient building with a large peristyle, probably built around the second century AD, in the southwest area of the archaeological site of Sidi Khiribech, in Berenike (modern Banghazi).",
